  Median coverage ratio over all apertures and thresholds: 1.13
  With 8 seeds each sd carries ~27% uncertainty, so this is CONSISTENT WITH UNITY.
  Read conservatively: the paired bootstrap is approximately correct, and
  the null's error bar is NOT the explanation for the 3.18.  The
  resolution of must-close item 2 rests on Sec. 4a-4b instead — the null
  is unbiased, the failing aperture moves between seeds, and 2 of 8 draws
  exceeding a max-over-36-correlated-tests criterion is unremarkable.
  A ratio meaningfully above 1 would need ~50 seeds to establish; that is
  not needed for this item and is not claimed.

